# Rule 1: a function returns a value, never a reference (read through any
# alias: the canonical return type).  const T and
# const T& are one value only while no reference into an argument escapes;
# the translation into System F erases references and cannot see a dangling
# one.  Exempt: the standard iterator protocol (a nested iterator or
# sentinel, by exact name), which Rule 3's folds run on.  Blind spot: decltype(auto) in a
# template pattern is undeduced and not seen.
match functionDecl(returns(hasCanonicalType(referenceType())), unless(anyOf(isImplicit(), isDefaulted(), isDeleted(), cxxMethodDecl(ofClass(cxxRecordDecl(isLambda()))), cxxMethodDecl(ofClass(cxxRecordDecl(matchesName("::(const_)?iterator$|::sentinel$")))))), isExpansionInMainFile(), hasAncestor(scope))
